# Wire contract declared in the bindings, not the layers above

Found and fixed in the 2026-08-25 review. Recorded because it is a
design decision, not just a fix.

## Problem

The sentence "StorePath and DerivedPath serialize, Value and
Derivation do not" was written out four times, by hand, in four
layers: grpc_schema._msg_arg_type, server.decode, server.encode and
remote.invoke. Each carried its own list of type names.

Adding a class meant editing all four. Forgetting one did not fail the
build: the schema fell through to Handle, the codec fell through to a
scalar table, and the first RPC touching the type died with a KeyError
from inside the server. The manifest already carried the `wire`
policy - the layers just did not use it.

That is the exact inverse of the goal: knowledge sitting at the top of
the stack, duplicated, instead of at the bottom, once.

## What the bindings declare now

    cdef class StorePath:
        _wire = "value"
        _wire_fields = (("base_name", "str"),)
        # plus _parts() / _from_parts()

    cdef class DerivedPath:
        _wire = "value"
        _wire_fields = (("path", "StorePath"), ("output", "str?"))

A field type may name another wire-value, which nests its message and
makes the codec recurse. A trailing "?" marks a field proto3 cannot
tell apart from its default - previously an `or None` hardcoded in two
places.

## What derives from it

- grpc_schema builds every value message from the declared fields. No
  type name appears in the module.
- ONE WireCodec, in huggorm/wire.py, serves both sides. It
  reads the manifest and nothing else. The two sides differ in exactly
  one respect - what a proxy handle means - so that is the one thing
  each passes in as a callback.
- server.py and remote.py name no domain type at all. A check in
  test_remote parses them and fails if one appears.

## Enforcement

The codegen refuses to ship a contradiction: a wire-value with no
fields, missing round-trip helpers, an unknown field type, a proxy
carrying fields, or a wire-value declared affine. That last one is the
interesting invariant - a value that may not leave its thread cannot
be serialized off it.

## Verification

Renaming `output` to `output_name` in store.pyx ALONE moved the proto
message, the server and the client together, suites green, no edit
above the bindings. Emptying _wire_fields failed the build with the
type named.

## Left for later

Method NAMING is generated (grpc_schema.annotate stamps req/resp/
service/path into the manifest), but Session's own rpcs are still
hand-built in grpc_schema. That is defensible - they are protocol, not
surface - but it means Session message shapes live in exactly the kind
of hand-written list this task removed elsewhere.
